## DESCRIPTION
## Calculate and reconcile the fee and reserve on a sold invoice.
## ENDDESCRIPTION
## KEYWORDS('business mathematics', 'percentages', 'invoice financing', 'proration')
## Author('Joe, Finofin AI assistant')
## Institution('Finofin')
## Level(2)
## TitleText1('The invoice reserve')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');
Context()->flags->set(tolType => 'absolute', tolerance => 0.005);

$face     = random(8, 14, 2) * 1000;
$advance  = random(70, 85, 5);
$rate     = random(1, 3, 1);
$days     = random(30, 60, 15);
$extra    = random(5, 15, 5);
$initial  = $face * $advance / 100;
$reserve  = $face - $initial;
$fee      = $face * $rate / 100 * $days / 30;
$released = $reserve - $fee;
$feeRise  = $face * $rate / 100 * $extra / 30;
$roundedRise = sprintf('%.2f', $feeRise);

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML
A repair shop sells a customer invoice with a face value of [$face] US dollars.
On the sale date a finance company pays the shop [$advance]% of the face value
and keeps the rest in reserve. For every 30 days until the customer pays, the
company charges [$rate]% of the full face value, prorated by the actual number
of days. It deducts this fee from the reserve and sends the balance to the shop.
Assume there are no other charges.

Enter each answer in US dollars, rounded to the nearest cent.

a. The customer pays after [$days] days. How much is the fee? [________]{$fee}

b. What additional cash does the shop receive from the reserve on the day the
customer pays? [________]{$released}

c. Suppose the customer had paid [$extra] days later. By how many dollars
would the cash received from the reserve have fallen? [________]{$feeRise}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a. The fee is based on the full invoice. Multiply [$face] by [$rate]/100 and by
[$days]/30 to get [$fee] dollars.

b. The shop already received [$initial] dollars at funding. The gross reserve
is therefore [$reserve] dollars. After deducting the fee, the finance company
releases [$released] dollars. As a check, the initial advance and the release
sum to the face value less the fee.

c. The initial advance stays fixed. The additional fee is [$face] times
[$rate]/100 times [$extra]/30. The release would fall by [$roundedRise] dollars.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
